  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 15 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 10/L10): spawn_session's authored max_iterations argument (1-128) is REFUSED, never clamped, with three distinct oracle-authored messages for three distinct bad-value classes: explicit null (\"...not null\", distinguished from ABSENT, which is silently fine and inherits the default), non-integer/bool/string (same message as each other, no range mentioned), and an out-of-range integer (range message with the offending value interpolated). Each of the three spawn_session calls is refused by validation BEFORE core.spawn is ever reached, so this costs zero upstream child calls and zero subsession registry rows — only the parent's own three tool round trips plus its final text. Exactly the observable a unit test cannot prove: the candidate's own validateMaxIterations tests (tests/orchestration-validation.test.ts) already verify the CANDIDATE's belief about the oracle's three messages; only the wire proves the oracle actually says this.",
